  "broader": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/puc/2004",
  "definition": "Revocation of Registration of CEPS or Aggregator",
  "effectiveDate": "2026-05-13",
  "expirationDate": "2036-05-13",
  "historyNote": "#12372, eff 11-1-17; ss by #14576, eff 5-13-26, EXPIRES: 5-13-36 (formerly Puc 2005.04)",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Puc 2004.04",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/puc2000.html",
  "prefLabel": "Puc 2004.04 Revocation of Registration of CEPS or Aggregator",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 2004.04 Revocation of Registration of CEPS or Aggregator.\n\n(a) If the commission finds, after notice and an opportunity to be heard and after consideration of the factors described in Puc 2004.05, that a sanctionable event has occurred with respect to a CEPS or aggregator and that the interests of customers of the CEPS or aggregator would not be harmed by such action, the commission shall revoke the registration of the CEPS or aggregator.\n\n(b) Upon the issuance by the commission of an order under (a) above, the registration of the CEPS or aggregator shall be revoked and the CEPS or aggregator shall not provide service, either directly or indirectly, to any customers in the state with respect to the supply of electricity or the procurement of such supply from and after the effective date of revocation.\n\n(c) The CEPS or aggregator subject to a revocation order issued under (a) above shall make arrangements for all of its customer accounts to be transferred and provide prior written notice to customers of such transfers in compliance with the provisions of such order and the requirements of this chapter and En 2000. The CEPS or aggregator shall provide the commission and the department with written confirmation and supporting evidence that it has complied with the foregoing requirements.\n\nSource. #12372, eff 11-1-17; ss by #14576, eff 5-13-26, EXPIRES: 5-13-36 (formerly Puc 2005.04)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/puc2000.html"
